      "observed": "Both Ethernet ESD-protection devices have pin 5 (VP) explicitly left unconnected, while pin 2 (VN) is connected to GND. The parts are identified as TPD4E1U06DCKR and their channels are placed on the Ethernet pairs.",
      "expected": "Connect each protector's positive clamp/reference pin to the appropriate reference required by the selected ESD-protection part, rather than leaving it floating.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U4\") (value \"TPD4E1U06DCKR\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"316\") (name \"unconnected-(U4-VP-Pad5)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"364\") (name \"unconnected-(U23-VP-Pad5)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"80\") (name \"GND\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet pairs may lack the intended positive-side ESD clamp path, reducing protection against transients and potentially increasing the risk of damage or link faults.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: both Ethernet ESD-protection devices leave their VP reference pins unconnected. This likely compromises the intended transient-protection path on the Ethernet pairs."
}

